      "writtenOn": "2023-05-22T03:06:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This doesn\u0027t make a lot of sense in a number of ways :\n• The name suggests it will run on the handler thread but not wait. This is especially bad as there is `Activity#runOnUiThread` which posts and doesn\u0027t wait.\n• This doesn\u0027t allow passing a runnable that throws a checked exception, reducing the utility.\n• This transforms the exception into an assert fail, which obfuscates the error\n• I\u0027m not even sure there is sufficient memory barriers for the thread running this to observe the write – I think there is, but I\u0027m not completely sure.\n• We already have methods doing this that have none of these drawbacks.\n\nYou can use HandlerUtils.visibleOnHandlerThread. That\u0027s what you need right ? You need the runnable to do something and that effect to be *visible* on the handler thread ? If not, you can have a wrapper with a more appropriate name, since the method *does* what you need apparently.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 145,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 145,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "dd6544388058c1fa2fda2353a1b0a26b07b2f943",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
