      "writtenOn": "2023-05-22T03:06:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do this in a member ? This looks error-prone.\n\nOne thing you could, which would be much nicer, is to change visibleOnHandlerThread to take a ThrowingProducer\u003cT\u003e instead of a ThrowingRunnable and have it return the value. I wish I had thought of this when I wrote it but now that I see your code it\u0027s pretty obvious.\n\nThen you can remove the member completely and say\n\n    private ... {\n      setUptimeMillis(time);\n      return visibleOnHandlerThread(() -\u003e mKeepaliveStatsTracker.buildKeepaliveMetrics();\n    }",
