      "side": 1,
      "message": "AssertionError is not something you\u0027re supposed to catch in a test : it means you\u0027re catching the result of a fail(), which makes no sense. This is because you\u0027re calling fail() with the actual exception instead of throwing it. You should have thrown it so you can actually test that it\u0027s the exception you expect. This will be solved when you use visibleOnHandlerThread instead",
